# x5_graph_clear: drop each graph value after its last consumer. On x4's peak.
#
# object     p_census_peak_x4 (owner census):
#              356,302,848 B  n=2   unowned torch.int64 (28996, 768)   embedding shares, twice
#               90,660,864 B  n=5   graph_param                        float32 originals, module-held
#                2,359,296 B  n=1   unowned torch.float32 (768, 768)
#            445 MB of ~1,053 MB; the int64 copies sit in Graph.forward's values dict.
# prior null 0.02% twice on the whole-model program (peak = ONNX conversion, before Graph.forward). This
#            arm's peak is inside the forward pass. Parallel test: SHAFT-GPU s3_param_spill_graphclear.
# free       no value dropped before its last consumer; graph outputs excluded. Upstream
#            _clear_unused_values() call commented out (cubic); the counter computes it once per value.
# gate       identical expected.
# expected   up to -356 MB, 750 to 920 MB (-15% to -30%); x4 spread 0.03%. Retired endpoint 643,784 kB.
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_stream_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu,graph_clear_values_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
